Do not serve the port-forward API to the guest

Upstream serves its control API inside the virtual network at
gatewayIP:80 so a VM can request port forwards. For sandbox the guest is
the untrusted party, and reaching that endpoint needs no credential.

A sandbox with no allow rules -- one sandbox reports as reaching nothing
-- could POST to /services/forwarder/expose and open a listener on the
host at *:19099, on every interface rather than loopback, forwarded to a
service of its own choosing. The host could then reach it, and so could
anything else on the network. `sandbox ports` showed nothing, correctly,
because sandbox had published nothing.

Ports are published from the host with -p. The guest does not get a say.

